  "query_preview": "..The main story will be the HOT temperatures through \nThursday, with high temperatures 5-9 degrees above normal and highs \ntopping out between 104-111 degrees. The Extreme Heat Warning has \nnow been extended through Thursday. Major HeatRisk is expected in \nthe warning area, which includes the Tucson Metro, San Pedro River \nValley, the Upper Gila River Valley and eastern Pinal County. For \nmore information on the Extreme Heat Warning, please refer to the \nPHXNPWTWC product.  \n\nOtherwise, high pressure aloft currently centered over western New \nMexico into far west Texas will shift slowly southeast into the Big \nBend area of Texas by early Friday. Flow around the high will import \nmoisture into the area, with PWATs rising to over an inch areawide \nlate Wednesday and Thursday. This will result in a slight chance of \nthunderstorms Wednesday mainly east/southeast of Tucson, with \nthunderstorm chances from Tucson eastward Thursday, retreating to \nfar eastern areas on Friday as a system moves to our north. Some of \nthese storms will be capable of producing gusty outflow winds to 40+ \nmph. \n  \nA strong upper low then moves into the Pacific Northwest on Friday, \nmoving across the northern Great Basin over the weekend. This system \nwill bring drying conditions and increasing southwest winds to the \narea starting Friday afternoon and continuing through Sunday. \nAfternoon/evening wind speeds of 15-20 mph and gusts to 30-35 mph \nmay lead to fire weather concerns over this period, especially on \nSaturday. High temperatures lower to near normal by Sunday.\n\nBy early next week, the upper high rebuilds over central Texas, with \nbaggy troughiness along the West Coast. Moisture flowing northward \nbetween these two features will move back into eastern portions of \nArizona, resulting in a slight chance of showers/thunderstorms east \nof Tucson. High temperatures remain around normal levels early next \nweek.",
